### Page 2 of 5

```text
Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
June 27, 2024
Access easements were increased to 80 feet and all lots are now served by more
than one access. Any development of the tracts for commercial use will require a site
plan planning action process. The subdivision is located in the LU zone district and no
zone change is included in the approval of the PDP application.
If the PDP is approved the next step for the applicant is to submit a subdivision permit
and plat application to Planning and Development and a Chapter 23 application to
WY DEQ. Mark Christensen, applicants agent, was present to answer questions.
Chairman Caughey opened the Public Hearing. Speaking in opposition of the project
were: Troy McLees, Steve Cooke, Eric Lundgren, and David Webster. Concerns
included lot sizes, undesignated commercial lots, averaging lot sizes using open
space, road maintenance, large inventory of unsold residential lots, contamination of
existing wells, and impacts to neighborhood from future commercial developments.
Hearing no further comments the public hearing was closed.
Responses to concerns included: new technology for small lot septic systems, D.E.O.
and S.E.O. approval  prior to recordation of the Subdivision Plat, stricter S.E.O.
requirements for commercial wells than residential wells, alignment of Road 220
access meets Public Works request.
Chairman Caughey called for a motion and discussion. Chairman Caughey said that
he has been on the Planning Commission for six years and this development is
different than what is customarily seen but that this application meets Laramie County
Land Use Regulations and State Statutes. He understands the concerns of the
development of the larger lots but any commercial developments will be required to go
through the planning process for a Site Plan.
Mark Smith moved, seconded by John Watkins to approve the Cowboy
Kids at Ridley Ranch Preliminary Development Plan with one condition
and adopt the findings of fact a of the staff report. Vote 4-0.
Caughey, Stadel, Watkins, Smith
Aye:
Gaspar
Excused:
